{"name":"Spinach Soup","hex":"#6e750e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of species Spinacia oleracea of edible plants, or its leaves.","Any of numerous plants, or their leaves, which are used for greens in the same way Spinacia oleracea is or resemble it in some way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach"},{"term":"soup","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various dishes commonly made by combining liquids, such as water or stock, with other ingredients, such as meat and vegetables, that contribute the food value, flavor, and texture.","A serving of such a dish, typically in a bowl."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feed: to provide with soup or a meal.","To develop (film) in a (chemical) developing solution."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soup"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinach soup","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach soup is a soup prepared using spinach as a primary ingredient. A common dish around the world, the soup can be prepared as a broth-based or cream-based soup, and the latter can be referred to as \"cream of spinach soup.\" In China, a spinach and tofu soup is also known as \"emerald and white jade soup\"; spinach and tofu represent emerald and white jade respectively, and thus the spinach soup itself can be called \"emerald soup\". Fresh, canned or frozen spinach can be used, and the spinach can be used whole, puréed or chopped. Additional ingredients can include onion, green onion, carrot, celery, tomatoes, potatoes, lemon juice, olive oil, seasonings, salt and pepper. Spinach soup is typically served hot, but can also be served as a cold soup. Prior to being served, it can be topped or garnished with ingredients such as sour cream and crème fraîche."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Cream_of_spinach_soup_%28rotated%29.jpg/330px-Cream_of_spinach_soup_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach_soup","wikidata":"Q12219244"},{"title":"Spinach","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage. The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach","wikidata":"Q81464"},{"title":"Soup","blocks":[{"text":"Soup is a primarily liquid food, generally served warm or hot – though it is sometimes served chilled – made by cooking or otherwise combining meat or vegetables with stock, milk, or water. According to The Oxford Companion to Food, soup is the main generic term for liquid savoury dishes; others include broth, bisque, consommé, potage and many more."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Asparagus_soup_%28spargelsuppe%29.jpg/330px-Asparagus_soup_%28spargelsuppe%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soup","wikidata":"Q41415"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Creamy_spinach_soup.jpg/250px-Creamy_spinach_soup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Creamy_spinach_soup.jpg/500px-Creamy_spinach_soup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Creamy_spinach_soup.jpg/250px-Creamy_spinach_soup.jpg?utm_so